{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Landed for review — Gerrit change 1409, patchset 2\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1409 — `8390: report two parents dropped in silence`\n\n## Gates (real exit codes, all from the worktree venv)\n\n| gate | exit |\n|---|---|\n| `make lint` (ruff check + format-check) | **0** |\n| `make typecheck` (mypy, 434 files) | **0** |\n| `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q` | **0** — 10240 passed, 38 skipped, 0 failed |\n| `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` | **0** — resolved 8390 |\n| `rebar review-plan 8390 --status` | `certified` |\n\n`gerrit/main` had moved past the base (`18f08d5` -> `7f09a32`: 846b + c6c9, touching only\n`llm/plan_review` and `llm/code_review`). Rebased LOCALLY rather than relying on server-side rebase\n(bug 3787) — no conflicts, disjoint files — and re-ran all three gates on the rebased tree; the\nnumbers above are the post-rebase run.\n\n## Files in the change (14)\n\n**The two fixes** — `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py` (`suppressed_out`),\n`outbound_differ.py` (the CREATE arm judges + forwards the sink),\n`adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py` (slot 4 records `outbound-parent-rejected`).\n**Port + implementations** — `_backend.py`, `adapters/jira/backend.py` (forwards),\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py` (accepts and ignores).\n**Docs / comments** — `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (AC5: the DC case),\n`dispatch_one.py` (comment only), `docs/env-vars.md` (regenerated: two shifted line numbers).\n**Tests** — the new `diffing/test_parent_drop_parity_8390.py`, plus signature-only updates to the\nthree `OutboundMapper` doubles (`backend_support.py`, `test_backend_neutrality.py`,\n`diffing/test_canonical_outbound_equivalence.py`).\n**One unplanned file** — `outbound_labels.py`. `outbound_differ.py` sat at 798 of the LOCKED 800-LOC\ncap, less headroom than any form of this change costs. The self-contained label-diff cluster moved\nthere VERBATIM (all four names diffed against HEAD and byte-identical) and is re-exported, so\n`outbound_differ.<name>` still resolves; this is the same seam-extraction the comment, link and\nassignee clusters already went through in that file.\n\n## Cloud-observable behaviour: UNCHANGED\n\nNo payload, no request, and no return value differs on any surface. Every addition writes to an\nobservability sink or is an out-parameter that never influences the mapped dict. The 8b25 guard is\nNOT lifted — rebar still declines to write a parent the tracker would reject or silently ignore. DC\nis doubly unaffected: `_map_local_to_dc_fields` never maps a parent, so its ignored `suppressed_out`\ncan never be appended to, and DC does not route through the ACLI path at all.\n\n## Step 7 sweeps\n\n**Construct axis** — swept every outbound parent write path. `dispatch_one._update_one_apply_parent`\nrecords on all three arms; DC's `_hierarchy.set_parent` raises `NotImplementedError`, which\n`dispatch_one` maps to `outbound-parent-unrepresentable` and records; Cloud's `acli.set_parent` has no\nswallow of its own. With slots 2 and 4 closed, no remaining path drops a parent without a record.\nOne RESIDUAL noted and NOT fixed: `acli_cli_ops.create_issue` skips the attach when `client is None`\nor the created key is missing, silently. Both are unreachable on the live path — `acli.py:325` always\npasses `client=self`, and `_create_issue_from_json` raises when the key is absent — so this is\n**accepted**, not filed: a defensive branch reachable only from fixtures.\n\n**Parity axis** — five-slot census. CLI (`rebar edit --parent`), MCP, and the library facade all write\nthe LOCAL store and reach the tracker only through the reconciler, so they inherit the fix rather than\nneeding their own; the automated-caller slot is the four reconciler surfaces, now all four covered;\nthe dual-direction slot is N/A — inbound writes go to the local store, where a write either lands or\nraises, so the \"never reached the tracker\" rule has no inbound counterpart.\n\n**NOT CLOSING this ticket** — awaiting `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on change 1409."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785903206463699001,"uuid":"9c3646ba-e2e6-4873-b454-87da70400d0c"}